{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The recurrence estimator is undefined: co-occurrence window, normalization, neighbor cap, popularity correction, and prefix support formula are missing. Global training-only statistics are allowed, but target-associated edges may create shortcuts that require explicit checks.",
    "Recency could mean position distance or elapsed time; the proposal does not specify which. Attention masks, empty histories, score scaling, parameter initialization, and a stateless way to pass causal context through the diagnostic interface also need concrete definitions.",
    "Candidate attention over every supervised prefix can require O(B L² K d) work for K candidates per position. Chunked inference alone does not establish training feasibility within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget.",
    "A zero residual coefficient initially blocks gradients to branch-exclusive parameters. The coefficient can still learn, but initialization and score scale determine whether the branch becomes useful or destabilizes training.",
    "No baseline validation HR@10, uncertainty assessment, or budgeted ablation schedule supports selecting this architecture over a simpler loss change. Originality 5, potential 8, and difficulty 5 are subjective; implementation difficulty may be understated.",
    "Candidate similarity and co-occurrence may reinforce broad affinity, popularity, or redundant recommendations—the failures being targeted. Simulator feedback from twenty users motivates a hypothesis but does not establish its generality or measure compatibility and unmet need."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify the recurrence mechanism, distinguish established components from novelty, and identify controls against popularity shortcuts.",
      "query": "In sequential recommendation using candidate-conditioned history attention, what reproducible methods define recency-biased attention and recurring-interest support from sparse item co-occurrence graphs? Compare normalized co-occurrence, popularity correction, causal prefix masking, and ablations separating candidate matching, recency, and recurrence; include DIN, temporal attention, and item-item collaborative filtering."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Determine whether the proposed residual can be trained and deployed within the budget while preserving identical causal scoring.",
      "query": "How can a SASRec candidate-conditioned attention residual be implemented efficiently for every supervised sequence position, with O(B L² K d) naive cost, and for chunked full-catalog inference? Look for exact batched causal masking, prefix computation reuse, numerically safe empty-history handling, and gradient behavior of a scalar residual gate initialized to zero."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Establish a credible comparison against simpler alternatives and address repeated selection on a small fixed validation sample.",
      "query": "What do gSASRec and studies of sampled recommendation evaluation establish about multi-negative BCE or generalized BCE versus sampled softmax, and about uncertainty and validation overfitting with HR@10 measured using 99 sampled negatives? Identify budget-matched ablations and paired user-level uncertainty estimates applicable to four datasets with 200 fixed validation users each."
    }
  ]
}
